Z||000011||Blondie88||10-25-2001||03:40 PM||||Well, exactly what you said.  I think United States employees are a lot more leniant about giving people without visas or green cards jobs.  They don't need to prove anything to the government.  In Winnemucca (my home town), there were actually meetings for the illegal immigrants telling them when immigration was coming, so they were off that day.  It's crazy!  I don't think it'll be like that in Canada.  Although I can always hope  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> hahaha i'd hate living a lie though...unless it was a really good paying lie.  j/k so i'd stay in buffalo! I might have to fly out there for an interview with an immigration officer sometime! Should be interesting, i've never been out that way. <P>But that's my blabber.  I'm going back to my blueberry muffin now.  Thanks muchos ||||reg||1
Z||000012||Tonker||10-26-2001||02:10 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Ken Wittlief:<BR><B>canadians can work wherever they want  here in the US, with two conditions<P> 1. if they loose their job they have 45 minutes to get out of the county.<P> 2. they have to wear a special hat that has a flashing red strobe light on top, so the US citizens cant tell from a distance of 2000', 'thats a canadian'<P> :c)<P> (they can work here)</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Ken, that's so much  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_bs.gif">. Let me assure you, as someone in the know (I recently had a business trip to California), that when you get to the border, US customs & immigrations officers intoduce themselves by giving you a full body cavity search(looking for contra-band maple syrup - very lucrative business here) and issue you a furry beaver-skin cap which reads "Howdy y'all I'm a Canajun!". Happily Americans are understanding enough to realise that red isn't a flattering colour for everybody and they allow you to choose from several different colours of strobe light.<P>In actuality when you lose a job, you have 30 minutes from the time you receive your notification to assemble and hitch up the dogsled team and make your way to the border. There you are divested of your cap and strobelight and subjected to another body cavity search( disgruntled Canadians have been known to try to smuggle back the Canada Geese that the Yanks steal from us every fall). Canadians found straggling for more than the allocated 30 minutes are usually sent to concentration camps in Utah, where they are forced to till the land and build roads.<P>As you can see we have a very close and open relationship with our American brothers to the South.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||12
